pt=1 -->\n**ard · triage:engineer · done**\n\nAdds in-cluster role image builds to the Kubernetes executor: a content-hash tag taken from the role directory at the pinned commit, a registry check, a budgeted builder pod, and a job pod pinned to the image digest. It also passes the agent base as a build arg on the Docker executor and updates the proposal. Size L, risk medium.\n\n## Open issues\n- The builder from #448 is a pod shape enforced by an admission policy, not a batch Job, so the plan builds with a pod.\n- Role Dockerfiles already take the agent base through an `AGENT_IMAGE` build arg, so the plan passes the `:latest` ghcr base as that arg instead of editing their `FROM` lines.\n- If the builder needs more RBAC than the chart grants, that change is under `deploy/`, which is a protected path and needs a human.\n- A private package looks the same as a missing one to the registry check, so the first build of each role is repeated until the package is made public.\n\nOutput: [.ard/449/triage-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/c30590700cd59a74157e6553972699d7d0fd09d0/.ard/449/triage-engineer.md) · log [.ard/449/logs/triage-engineer-20261126T083340.158Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/c30590700cd59a74157e6553972699d7d0fd09d0/.ard/449/logs/triage-engineer-20261126T083340.158Z.log) · job `01M8BFT9TWMTADCE5ECJKF4AC0` · attempt 1\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-26T08:35:14Z\n\n<!-- ard:triage gate=approval job=01M8BFS7QD9NFYVSTX882SMBRY -->\n**ard · triage · ready for approval**\n\nTriage is complete; the plan is in `.ard/449/plan.md`. A maintainer adds `ard:approved` to start the `engineer` worker. An approval given before triage finished does not count: remove and re-add the label.\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-26T09:04:55Z\n\n<!-- ard:closeout job=01M8BGQ5GQHEJ2AXEP2GZH47NE attempt=1 -->\n**ard · worker:engineer · needs-human**\n\nThe Kubernetes executor now builds a role's Dockerfile in the cluster and runs the job on the resulting image, pinned by digest, instead of ignoring the Dockerfile. The image tag is a content hash of the role directory at the pinned role SHA, so an unchanged role is built once.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/executor/kube/roleimage.go` (new): `RoleImages` options, `RoleTree` (git `ls-tree`/`archive` in the controller clone at the pinned SHA, never the worktree), tag `h-<hash>`, registry check (401/403/404 mean not built, other errors fail as a registry check), single-flight per tag, builder pod in the shape the #448 admission policy admits, wait within a budget, typed `ErrRoleImageBuild` causes (exit code and redacted log tail, timeout, refused pod, no digest), and cleanup of pod and Secret.\n- `kube.go`, `pod.go`: `Prepare` builds before the worktree exists and sets the image; with `RoleImages` nil it still logs `kube.dockerfile_ignored`. The agent container uses the handle's image; the pre and post containers keep the pod image.\n- `api/types.go`: AppArmor profile field.\n- `internal/cli`, `internal/servecmd/serve.go`: `--k8s-build-namespace`, `--k8s-builder-image`, `--k8s-builder-uid`, `--k8s-role-image-repository`, `--k8s-role-image-push-secret` (and the `ARD_K8S_*` env the chart sets). Images are on only when the build namespace is set; partial settings or an undigested builder image are errors.\n- `internal/executor/local/docker.go`: `--build-arg AGENT_IMAGE=<agent image>` when one is configured.\n- `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/runbooks/role-images.md`: the k8s behaviour, and the `:latest` base residual risk (already recorded, now tied to the build).\n- Tests: `roleimage_test.go` (tag stability, cached, success and pod shape, SHA-only context, private package, registry down, failure with redaction, timeout, admission denied, bad digest, single-flight, rejects, real-git check), `k8s_test.go`, `agentimage_test.go`.\n\n## Testing\n`make lint` passes. `go test ./...` passes (including `-race` on the kube package).\n\n## Open issues\n- The builder command (`buildctl-daemonless.sh`, `/dev/termination-log` metadata file, `DOCKER_CONFIG` mount, `--oci-worker-no-process-sandbox`) has not been run against a real cluster or the pinned BuildKit image; only the fake client covers it.\n- The plan says a Secret first, then the pod. I create the pod first, then the Secret owned by it (as `buildSecret` does for job pods), so a refused pod leaves no Secret.\n- The role path must be `.ard/<scanners|triage|workers|reviewers>/<name>`; other paths are rejected for builds.\n- No `deploy/` change was needed.\n\n`log withheld: secret scan flagged it (rules: generic-assignment)`\n\nPR: [#452](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/pull/452)\nTests: passed\nOutput: [.ard/449/worker-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/e9a495df1141abf032dc3b37fa0ebc87e3f18463/.ard/449/worker-engineer.md) · log withheld (secret scan) · job `01M8BGQ5GQHEJ2AXEP2GZH47NE` · attempt 1\n\n\n.ard:\n138\n142\n157\n158\n159\n160\n161\n165\n168\n174\n178\n184\n194\n203\n204\n205\n212\n213\n215\n216\n217\n221\n222\n223\n224\n227\n231\n236\n237\n238\n239\n241\n242\n243\n244\n245\n247\n252\n254\n255\n267\n268\n276\n277\n292\n293\n297\n298\n299\n300\n301\n302\n304\n305\n306\n307\n312\n313\n314\n315\n316\n317\n318\n321\n322\n323\n332\n333\n334\n335\n336\n337\n338\n339\n340\n344\n345\n346\n347\n348\n349\n350\n355\n357\n366\n384\n385\n386\n387\n388\n394\n396\n40\n402\n406\n407\n41\n410\n411\n413\n414\n415\n416\n42\n426\n43\n435\n44\n440\n441\n449\n45\n47\n48\n49\n50\n51\n52\n56\n58\n59\n61\n89\nconfig.yaml\nreviewers\nscanners\ntriage\nworkers\n\n.ard/449:\ncosts\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WvpysCpSbhn9C7Xios5BCY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
